Alas, all the possible world notions are themselves intensional (they are 
*possible* worlds after all), so this doesn't help with an extensional 
reading.  I am inclined at the moment to go with questions as a primitive 
notion and take two things that successfully answer (are true members of) the 
same question as being intersubstitutable.  But even as I say this I start 
seeing problems, so I am gong to pass for this round.
           
